-- generator, not hand-typed), and seeding the six module quiz banks plus the
-- final exam. Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- Six modules, 28 lessons: one model two blocks, the census, control points
-- cross the fault, the trend plane, simple kriging, and per-block volume and
-- the workflow.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the earthmodel teaching oracle in
-- src/lib/earthmodelTeaching.js (labelBlocks / planeFit / simpleKrige /
-- zoneVolumes over the golden model) and reproduces the live advanced
-- capstone answer key: block 1 node count 174 (tol 0, hand-countable as
-- 9x12 + 11x6), trend porosity at (1250, 2250) 0.3075 (hand-exact from the
-- recovered plane 0.38 - 0.00004x - 0.00001y), kriged porosity at (1500,
-- 2500) 0.2914277719922997, kriged porosity AT W1 0.315 (the honor-the-data
-- exactness, tol 0.0005), zone A weighted porosity in block 0
-- 0.28631191845445614, and zone A bulk in block 1 13.998749999999998e6 m3.
-- populationLab.test.js pins the panel math to the same values.
--
-- Tier positioning: DC12 owns the container and forward-quotes the census
-- 326/174 and the block volumes 31.00125 + 13.99875 = 45e6; DC28 owns the
-- trajectories that put W2's zone A control point at x 1610.8719179395334.
-- This tier owns the consequences: W2's wellhead is in block 1 but its data
-- is in block 0 (the fault at x 1575 lies between, margin 35.87 m), so block
-- 1 is a one-well block whose kriged map is the constant 0.315 at any valid
-- nugget; the trend fit is EXACT on this fixture because the data was built
-- on a plane (a property of the data, not evidence for the method); kriging
-- relaxes to the ARITHMETIC mean 0.2905162808206047 while the constant
-- method uses the WEIGHTED 0.2903935560727246 (two means, one engine); and
-- per-block volumes close to literally zero because each node adds into its
-- block register and the total register in one pass.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and checked
-- for cyclic key sequences, answer-index skew, within-pool near-duplicates and
-- same-claim option pairs before seeding. Across the 132 questions the correct
-- option is longest in 15 pct and shortest in 1 pct.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first insert;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on
-- re-seeds.
--
-- Ladder note: an ADVANCED enrollment needs an unrevoked PROFESSIONAL
-- certification on the SAME app, so the dry-run probes back-stop an earthmodel
-- professional cert in-transaction, and P3b checks prove BOTH tiers below are
-- left undisturbed at 132 questions each.
--
-- New em-population-explorer panel. NO DDL. Data only.
-- ============================================================================

values ('earthmodel', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-one-model-two-blocks","title":"One Model, Two Blocks","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-the-fault-polygon","l03-labelling-the-nodes","l04-the-population-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-the-census","title":"The Census","lesson_keys":["l01-hand-counting-174","l02-area-is-not-a-census","l03-the-closure-key","l04-what-a-block-means"]},{"key":"m03-control-points-cross-the-fault","title":"Control Points Cross the Fault","lesson_keys":["l01-where-control-points-live","l02-w2-crosses","l03-one-value-is-not-a-statistic","l04-weights-are-measured-depth"]},{"key":"m04-the-trend-plane","title":"The Trend Plane","lesson_keys":["l01-a-plane-through-the-points","l02-an-exact-fit-is-a-property-of-the-data","l03-reading-the-coefficients","l04-extrapolation-has-no-floor","l05-trend-per-block"]},{"key":"m05-simple-kriging","title":"Simple Kriging","lesson_keys":["l01-the-variogram","l02-honoring-the-data","l03-the-nugget","l04-two-means-in-one-engine","l05-the-probe-value","l06-one-well-is-enough"]},{"key":"m06-per-block-volume-and-the-workflow","title":"Per-Block Volume and the Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-volumes-per-block","l02-the-hand-chain","l03-the-workflow-end-to-end","l04-the-capstone-walkthrough","l05-onward-from-earth-modeling"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
